e-002", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-04/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Under an earthen tumulus 19.5 m high and 76 m in diameter, the Tomb of Macridy Bey hides two vaulted chambers behind a facade of Ionic columns, already looted when it was excavated in 1910."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-04: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-04-check-002 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-04/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "earthen tumulus 19.5 m high [S4]; 76 m in diameter [S4]; two vaulted chambers [S4]; a facade of Ionic columns [S5]; already looted when excavated [S6]; excavated in 1910 [S6]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-04: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-04-verify-006 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-04/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The Tomb of Macridy Bey is an ancient Macedonian tomb in Greece (near Thessaloniki, Central Macedonia) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tomb_of_Macridy_Bey]; The tomb lies in Greece (Central Macedonia) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tomb_of_Macridy_Bey]; The tomb is covered by an earthen tumulus 19.5 m high and 76 m in diameter [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tomb_of_Macridy_Bey]; The tomb has two vaulted chambers (antechamber and burial chamber) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tomb_of_Macridy_Bey]; The chambers lie behind a facade of Ionic columns [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tomb_of_Macridy_Bey]; The tomb had already been looted when it was excavated in 1910 [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tomb_of_Macridy_Bey]"}]'::jsonb),
