b76b14dc9bef0733a6d39705a839fa55244c5002d162025f84c"}}'' restored on Mochlos', '53b2716285efcb76b14dc9bef0733a6d39705a839fa55244c5002d162025f84c', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-04: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-04-write-002", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-04/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Mochlos is a small, uninhabited island off eastern Crete, yet there is evidence it was a Minoan harbor joined to the mainland. Its hoards held copper ingots that isotopes trace to Cyprus."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-04: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-04-check-002 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-04/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "a small, uninhabited island [S1]; off eastern Crete [S1]; evidence it was a Minoan harbor [S2]; joined to the mainland [S2]; its hoards held copper ingots [S6]; isotopes trace the copper to Cyprus [S6]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-04: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-04-verify-006 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-04/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Mochlos is the archaeological site of an ancient Minoan settlement (central claim: a Minoan settlement site on an island off Crete) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mochlos]; Mochlos is a small island [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mochlos]; The island is uninhabited [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mochlos]; The island lies off eastern Crete (Gulf of Mirabello, 150 m from the Cretan coast) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mochlos]; There is evidence that in Minoan times Mochlos was not an island but was joined (attached) to the mainland [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mochlos]; Mochlos acted as a (Minoan) eastern harbor [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mochlos]; Metal hoards were excavated at Mochlos (Late Minoan I) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mochlos]; The hoards held copper ingots (oxhide ingots and fragments) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mochlos]; Isotope analyses trace the copper ingots to Cyprus [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mochlos]"}]'::jsonb),
