{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-04: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-04-check-005 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-04/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the ovens are at Vilassar de Dalt [S1]; they produced large ceramic materials industrially [S2]; study of the magnetic properties of ovens 1 and 2 helped date them [S3]; ovens 1 and 2 date to the 1st and 2nd centuries AD [S3]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-04: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-04-verify-015 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-04/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The Roman Ovens of the Fornaca are ancient Roman oven structures in the archaeological site of Fornaca at Vilassar de Dalt, Catalonia, Spain (central claim: a Roman kiln site at Vilassar de Dalt). [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_ovens_of_the_Fornaca]; The ovens fired large ceramic materials on an industrial scale. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_ovens_of_the_Fornaca]; The magnetic properties of ovens 1 and 2 (archaeomagnetic study) were used to help date them. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_ovens_of_the_Fornaca]; Ovens 1 and 2 are dated to the 1st and 2nd centuries AD. [SUPPORTED: https://ca.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forns_romans_de_la_Fornaca_de_Vilassar_de_Dalt]"}]'::jsonb),
