2026-09-27-04-write-005", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-04/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "On a ridgetop by the Messenian Gulf, Nichoria was a major outpost of Pylos and fell in the same event that claimed the palace there. At its acropolis foot, a burial circle held 7 people."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-04: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-04-check-005 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-04/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Nichoria is on a ridgetop by the Messenian Gulf [S1]; it was a major outpost of Pylos [S4]; it was destroyed in the same event that claimed the palace at Pylos [S5]; a burial circle lay at the foot of the acropolis [S7]; it held 7 people [S7]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-04: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-04-verify-015 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-04/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Nichoria is a (Mycenaean-era) settlement site in Messenia, on a ridgetop at the northwestern corner of the Messenian Gulf, Greece (central claim). [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nichoria]; Nichoria was a major outpost of Pylos. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nichoria]; Nichoria fell (was destroyed) in the same event that claimed the palace at Pylos. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nichoria]; Nichoria''s destruction coincided with that of the Palace of Nestor (Pylos), c. 1200 BC (second source). [SUPPORTED: https://www.efamess.gr/en/pois/karpofora-nichoria/]; A burial circle was found at the foot of the Nichoria acropolis. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nichoria]; The burial circle held 7 people. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nichoria]"}]'::jsonb),
