: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-04-write-005", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-04/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "On a hill spur above the Fowey valley, Largin Castle holds one enclosure inside another: an outer rampart and ditch entered from the south, an inner oval offset to the north."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-04: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-04-check-005 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-04/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "on a hill spur above the Fowey valley [S2]; an outer rampart and ditch enclosure [S4]; entered from the south [S4]; an inner oval enclosure lies inside it [S5]; the inner oval is offset to the north [S5]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-04: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-04-verify-015 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-04/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Largin Castle is a hillfort (a fortified enclosure) in Cornwall, England (central claim: an Iron Age contour hillfort). [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Largin_Castle]; It lies on a hill spur above the Fowey valley. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Largin_Castle]; The hillfort has an outer enclosure formed by a rampart and ditch. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Largin_Castle]; The outer enclosure is entered from the south. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Largin_Castle]; Within the outer enclosure lies a smaller inner enclosure of oval shape, also defined by ramparts and ditch (one enclosure inside another). [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Largin_Castle]; The inner oval enclosure is offset to the north. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Largin_Castle]"}]'::jsonb),
