ic site of prehistoric human habitation, gave up cave paintings, flint knives, arrowheads, bone combs and boards whose dents suggest wheat was milled on them."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-04: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-04-check1-001 (check1), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-04/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the site is Zar Cave [S1]; it is an Upper Paleolithic site [S1]; it is a site of prehistoric human habitation [S1]; cave paintings were found there [S3]; flint knives were found there [S4]; arrowheads were found there [S4]; bone combs were found there [S4]; boards with traces of dents were found there [S5]; the dents suggest that wheat was milled on the boards [S5]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-04: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-04-verify-015 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-04/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Zar Cave is a cave in the southern part of Zar village, Kalbajar District, Azerbaijan (central claim: a cave archaeological site). [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zar_Cave]; Zar Cave is an archaeological site of prehistoric human habitation. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zar_Cave]; The site dates to the Upper Paleolithic. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zar_Cave]; Cave paintings were found at Zar Cave. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zar_Cave]; Flint knives were found at Zar Cave. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zar_Cave]; Arrowheads were found at Zar Cave. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zar_Cave]; Bone combs were found at Zar Cave. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zar_Cave]; Boards bearing traces of dents were found at Zar Cave. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zar_Cave]; The dents on the boards suggest that wheat was milled on them. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zar_Cave]"}]'::jsonb),
